NAME
     memck - check memory, clock and vector state across a crossing

SYNOPSIS
     memck [MB] [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
     memck fills MB megabytes (default 16) of memory with a pattern keyed
     by the address and, once a second for SECONDS, verifies all of it,
     checks that the clock has not gone back and that it advances at the
     rate of the ticks, and checksums a set of vector registers it holds.
     One line per round; a mismatch is fatal and names its address. It is
     the oracle the crossing tests start before a move and read after it.

SEE ALSO
     cksum(1), vhold(1), zerocheck(1)
